The four videos are H.264, yuv420p, 1920x1080, 30 frames per second, with no audio stream (ffprobe lists one stream, of type video), and have the moov atom before mdat (faststart). Lengths: 1-deploy-upgrade.mp4 0:35 (35.3 s), 2-component-overrides.mp4 0:45 (45.0 s), 3-backup-restore.mp4 1:08 (68.1 s), 4-clone.mp4 1:08 (67.6 s), all 3:00 or less (SC-002). The four files have modification times between 14:16:08Z and 14:56:18Z, so this run wrote all four.

The demos check their own results and fail otherwise:

- demo 1 fails unless the upgrade task lists the step of the driver's upgrade action as succeeded (check_upgrade_action in scenarios/deploy_upgrade.py);
- demo 3 fails unless Infrahub lists sw2 and Semaphore lists the template "List network devices" after the restore (check_listed in scenarios/backup_restore.py);
- demo 4 fails unless the task logs give 2, 3 and 2 devices (check_device_count in scenarios/clone.py).

All four demos were recorded, so each of these checks passed. The videos of this run were not watched.

